{"base_rate":0.06666666666666667,"brier":0.043675315315315315,"bss":0.2980752895752896,"bss_hi":0.4790318584450663,"bss_lo":-0.06001630326151826,"chart":{"base":[148.4,152.4],"fp":[180.1,162.3],"lead":"62,284.8 272,262.2 482,233.6 692,179.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.30 — higher than 48% of cities","fp":"low end +0pp, high end +30pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 100% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 0%; promised 30% → rained 31%"},"rel":"64.1,464 248.5,331"},"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.00954954954954955,"ess":314.9274827925269,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Phoenix</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Phoenix rain forecast is moderately skilful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (48%), believe about\n<b>51%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 555 days, 2024-05-01 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPHOENIX AP ASOS BACKUP, 4.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.30, ranked 70 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(20&ndash;129) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>361</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Phoenix</b> <span class=\"muted\">US</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.30</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>20&ndash;129\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>555 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Phoenix &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Phoenix\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 64.25975609756098,364.2439024390244 94.17236363636363,315.8181818181818 228.97578947368422,164.87719298245617 228.97578947368422,247.89473684210526 94.17236363636363,368.76363636363635 64.25975609756098,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"357.73333333333335\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"357.73333333333335\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,379.98337950138506 64.25975609756098,382.0 94.17236363636363,342.2909090909091 228.97578947368422,196.80701754385964\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 361 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"379.98337950138